      {"@type":"Question","name":"Is running a sustainable event a legal requirement?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Increasingly. Single-use-plastic rules, strict waste law (such as EU and AGEC law in the French West Indies), and permit conditions near protected reefs and turtle beaches all apply."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"Do sponsors care about sustainability?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Credible eco credentials attract sponsors, press and public funding under ESG expectations; greenwashing is penalised."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"Do attendees prefer eco-friendly events?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — audiences increasingly choose events on sustainability, which lifts ticket appeal and loyalty."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"How does sustainability improve event resilience?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Efficient water, energy and waste systems cut exposure to the climate and supply-chain shocks that hit islands first."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"Why does sustainability matter for a Caribbean venue specifically?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Caribbean events often sit metres from coral reefs, mangroves and turtle-nesting beaches; low-impact operations protect the very setting that draws the crowd."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"How does going eco strengthen an event's relationship with its community?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Prioritising local vendors, artists and an NGO partnership builds goodwill and a community licence to operate that keeps the event welcome year after year."}}
